zink: no push descriptors on MoltenVK

MoltenVK copies the descriptor data of every push into its command
buffer (MVKCmdPushDescriptorSetWithTemplate::setContent), which took
30-40 % of zink's driver thread in OpenMW. Treat MoltenVK like AMD in
the existing driver-id quirk, so descriptors go through zink's regular
descriptor sets. Measured on an iPad Pro (M1): zink driver thread
-39 % CPU, frame times unchanged. Other drivers are unaffected.

Upstream: not submitted.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -3011,6 +3011,10 @@
       screen->info.have_KHR_push_descriptor = false;
       /* Interpolation is not consistent between two triangles of a rectangle. */
       screen->driver_workarounds.inconsistent_interpolation = true;
+      break;
+   case VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK:
+      /* MoltenVK copies the descriptor data of every push into the command buffer: costly per draw */
+      screen->info.have_KHR_push_descriptor = false;
       break;
    default:
       break;
